  "presentation_summary": [
    "A 49-year-old man presented to the emergency room with sudden dyspnea on the day of admission.",
    "He did not report cough, purulent sputum, or fever, but had poor oral hygiene with extensive dental caries.",
    "Presentation vitals showed temperature 36.1 C, blood pressure 130/70 mmHg, respiratory rate 35/min, heart rate 120/min, and oxygen saturation 76% on room air.",
    "Despite 15 L/min oxygen by face mask he rapidly developed acute respiratory failure and was mechanically ventilated.",
    "Labs showed WBC 17.94 x10^9/L with 90.1% neutrophils, hemoglobin 11.1 g/dL, platelets 589 x10^9/L, ESR 105 mm/hr, CRP 275.6 mg/L, creatinine 1.86 mg/dL, and mild cholestatic liver test abnormalities.",
    "Initial chest radiograph showed left lower-lung consolidation; CT showed a large left lower lung abscess with internal air, surrounding consolidation, and an air-fluid level."
